      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0a085860c80a2aebafcf45ba3b2c30fc?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FFA-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "frank asseg",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a48a5426330072ea6384",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "As discussed in yesterday's committer call i conducted some tests with the Java API and Joda Time:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Java API I                      55593.13 ns",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Java API II                       5386.17 ns",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Joda Time I                    51827.76 ns",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Joda Time II                     9197.76 ns",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The tests marked \"I\" have been constructing a DateFormatter for each parsing cycle, while the tests marked with \"II\" have been reusing an instance.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Since Java's SimpleDateFormat is not thread safe the \"Java API II\" test is not eligible for usage in fedora but was added for comparison.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Since JodaTime's DateFormatter is thread-safe \"Joda Time II\" seems a valid way to improve the performance a slight bit and decreasing object allocation.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "I'll implement a DateUtil using JodaTime and send Adam a request for review.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
