      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>As discussed in yesterday's committer call i conducted some tests with the Java API and Joda Time:</p>\n\n<p>Java API I                      55593.13 ns<br/>\nJava API II                       5386.17 ns<br/>\nJoda Time I                    51827.76 ns<br/>\nJoda Time II                     9197.76 ns</p>\n\n<p>The tests marked \"I\" have been constructing a DateFormatter for each parsing cycle, while the tests marked with \"II\" have been reusing an instance.<br/>\nSince Java's SimpleDateFormat is not thread safe the \"Java API II\" test is not eligible for usage in fedora but was added for comparison.<br/>\nSince JodaTime's DateFormatter is thread-safe \"Joda Time II\" seems a valid way to improve the performance a slight bit and decreasing object allocation.<br/>\nI'll implement a DateUtil using JodaTime and send Adam a request for review.</p>",
     "created": "26/Oct/12 11:50 AM",
